        "iterations": 100,
        "explanation": "Computational Complexity Analysis (GEMM Operations):\nThe backward pass performs approximately double the dense matrix multiplications (GEMM) of the forward pass:\n  - Forward Pass requires 3 Matrix Multiplications:\n      1. Z1 = X @ W1\n      2. Z2 = A1 @ W2\n      3. Z3 = A2 @ W3\n  - Backward Pass requires 5 Matrix Multiplications:\n      1. dW3 = A2.T @ dZ3   (gradient w.r.t. parameters W3)\n      2. dA2 = dZ3 @ W3.T   (gradient backpropagated to activations A2)\n      3. dW2 = A1.T @ dZ2   (gradient w.r.t. parameters W2)\n      4. dA1 = dZ2 @ W2.T   (gradient backpropagated to activations A1)\n      5. dW1 = X.T @ dZ1    (gradient w.r.t. parameters W1)\nBecause backpropagation must evaluate both parameter gradients (for weight updates) and activation gradients\n(for error transmission across layers), it requires significantly more floating-point operations (FLOPs)."
